e default AdviceMode.PROXY (the current test only uses AdviceMode.ASPECTJ, which doesn't need CGLIB), those would need their own proxy classes added to the same predefinition generator.\",\n  \"risks\": [\n    \"The predefinition workaround relies on CGLIB's debug-location dump landing exactly on the native-image build classpath before analysis; if class naming/hashing changes in a later spring-aspects/spring-core patch, the generator's expected-class-file check will need updating.\",\n    \"Only the AdviceMode.ASPECTJ-based aspects and the @EnableSpringConfigured path were verified; any newly added test exercising proxy-based (CGLIB) advice modes would need the same predefinition treatment or it will hit the identical runtime-class-definition error.\"\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":9097,"type":"result","duration_ms":306756,"uuid":"87da2a1d-4032-4e6d-a428-2c557fd82221","ttft_stream_ms":1536,"time_to_request_ms":69,"first_content_frame_ms":1537,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}

